   :enums
   #:tension{:status #{:refuted :carried :cashed :dissolved},
             :born-of
             #{:refuted-rationale
               :build-event
               :operator-dictation
               :refused-prediction}},
   :rules
   ["poles are exactly two, both non-blank -- a tension with one pole is a plan"
    ":tension/statement is verbatim from :tension/statement-source. For :born-of :refused-prediction the statement-source IS the in-record :tension/refusal field (a machine-born tension has no dictated text; the typed refusal is the primary source) and the statement must be the refusal read back verbatim as data -- control 12 enforces this mechanically; external pointers are context and live in :provenance"
    ":tension/status is the status AT MINT and must equal the type of the mint event"
    ":tension/pattern-links [] means no graduation is claimed; the birth rule proposes and a person writes"]},
  :event
  {:required
   [:event/id
    :event/seq
    :event/tension
    :event/type
    :event/at
    :event/by
    :event/evidence],
   :optional [:event/row :event/note :event/to-status],
   :enums
   #:event{:type
           #{:evidence-added :refuted :carried :cashed :dissolved}},
   :rules
   ["every tension has exactly one :carried mint event, and it is that tension's lowest :event/seq"
    "a status-moving event (:cashed/:refuted/:dissolved) requires a non-empty :event/evidence AND an :event/row -- section 3's 'status moves only with a pointer to the cashing/refuting row'"
    ":evidence-added never moves status; it is how a fact that bears on a carried tension is recorded without ruling on it"
    ":event/seq is unique and ascending across the whole ledger; events are appended, never rewritten"
    "no status-moving event may follow a terminal one (:cashed/:refuted/:dissolved) for the same tension"]}},
